---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
const lang = 'en';
---

<DocsLayout lang={lang}>
  <h1 class="font-mono text-3xl font-bold text-mono-50">CLI</h1>
  <p class="mt-4 text-mono-400 leading-relaxed">
    The <code class="text-mono-200">roamy</code> CLI is a terminal session manager that communicates with roamyd over a Unix domain socket (local) or WebSocket (remote).
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Commands</h2>
  <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/50 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-mono-300"><code>roamy &lt;program&gt; [args...]     Launch program in a managed session
roamy shell                   Launch default shell ($SHELL)
roamy list                    List active sessions
roamy join &lt;session-id&gt;       Reattach to existing session
roamy kill &lt;session-id&gt;       Terminate a session
roamy daemon start|stop|status  Manage roamyd daemon
roamy update [--open]         Check for updates (--open opens browser)
roamy help                    Show help
roamy version                 Show version</code></pre>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Session Lifecycle</h2>
  <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6 text-sm text-mono-400">
    <li><strong class="text-mono-200">Create</strong> &mdash; <code class="text-mono-200">roamy shell</code> or <code class="text-mono-200">roamy &lt;program&gt;</code> creates a new PTY-backed session via roamyd.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-mono-200">Attach</strong> &mdash; Your terminal enters raw mode and proxies I/O to the session. Scrollback is replayed on attach.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-mono-200">Detach</strong> &mdash; Press <kbd class="rounded border border-mono-700 bg-mono-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-mono-300">Ctrl+]</kbd> then <kbd class="rounded border border-mono-700 bg-mono-800 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs text-mono-300">d</kbd>. The session keeps running in the background.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-mono-200">Reattach</strong> &mdash; <code class="text-mono-200">roamy join &lt;id&gt;</code> reconnects to the session with scrollback replay.</li>
    <li><strong class="text-mono-200">Destroy</strong> &mdash; <code class="text-mono-200">roamy kill &lt;id&gt;</code> terminates the PTY process and removes the session.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Daemon Management</h2>
  <pre class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-mono-800 bg-mono-900/50 p-4 font-mono text-sm text-mono-300"><code>roamy daemon start   # Start roamyd in background
roamy daemon stop    # Send shutdown signal to roamyd
roamy daemon status  # Check if roamyd is running</code></pre>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    On <code class="text-mono-200">daemon start</code>, the CLI locates the <code class="text-mono-200">roamyd</code> binary (same directory as <code class="text-mono-200">roamy</code> executable, or PATH) and spawns it with <code class="text-mono-200">--daemon</code>. A non-blocking update check runs after the daemon starts.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Connection</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-mono-400">
    The CLI connects to roamyd via Unix domain socket on Unix (<code class="text-mono-200">$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/roamy/roamyd.sock</code> or <code class="text-mono-200">ROAMY_SOCKET</code>). On Windows, it connects via the TCP WebSocket endpoint.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-10 font-mono text-xl font-bold text-mono-100">Environment Variables</h2>
  <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="w-full text-sm text-mono-400">
      <thead><tr class="border-b border-mono-800 text-left"><th class="pb-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-200">Variable</th><th class="pb-2 font-mono text-mono-200">Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody class="divide-y divide-mono-800/50">
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>ROAMY_SOCKET</code></td><td class="py-2">UDS socket path (default: auto-detect, Unix only)</td></tr>
        <tr><td class="py-2 pr-6 font-mono text-mono-100"><code>SHELL</code></td><td class="py-2">Default shell for <code class="text-mono-200">roamy shell</code></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
